\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n@Path(\"/hello\")\r\nclass ExampleResource {\r\n    @GET\r\n    fun hello() = SomeInterface.staticMethod()\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nKotlin codes are compiled specified version.\r\nCan use new features depends specified version.\r\n\r\n**Actual behavior**\r\nKotlin codes are compiled JVM 1.6.\r\nCompiler rises RuntimeException.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. create java 1.8 project and define example classes.\r\n2. mvn compile quarkus:dev\r\n3. curl localhost:8080/hello\r\n4. change string.\r\n5. curl localhost:8080/hello\r\n\r\n**Configuration**\r\nnothing\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\nnothing\r\n\r\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\r\n - Output of `uname -a` or `ver`: Darwin PC-XXX.local 18.7.0 Darwin Kernel Version 18.7.0: Sun Dec  1 18:59:03 PST 2019; root:xnu-4903.278.19~1/RELEASE_X86_64 x86_64\r\n - Output of `java -version`: java version \"12.0.2\" 2019-07-16 Java(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build 12.0.2+10) Java HotSpot(TM) 64-Bit Server VM (build 12.0.2+10, mixed mode, sharing)\r\n - GraalVM version (if different from Java): openjdk version \"11.0.6\" 2020-01-14 OpenJDK Runtime Environment GraalVM CE 19.3.1 (build 11.0.6+9-jvmci-19.3-b07) OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM GraalVM CE 19.3.1 (build 11.0.6+9-jvmci-19.3-b07, mixed mode, sharing)\r\n - Quarkus version or git rev: 1.2.0.CR1\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nTo solve it, add `compilerArguments.setJvmTarget(context.getTargetJvmVersion());` here I think.\r\nhttps://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/8e06dad026794c31e49040950b9cf63947ebd284/extensions/kotlin/deployment/src/main/java/io/quarkus/kotlin/deployment/KotlinCompilationProvider.java#L39","closed_by":{"login":"machi1990","id":10106536,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTA2NTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10106536?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/machi1990","html_url":"https://github.com/machi1990","followers_url":"htt